            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Arika L Thomas"
            },
            "reviewBody": "really tasty! I only give it 4 stars because I modified it a bit. I used frozen mexican corn with blackbeans and added a little chili seasoning. It was aweswome! I did have to heat it longer and hotter than the recipe called for but it all came together in the end. a definite keeper!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BEDRESTMOM"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This dip is quite good, but the fat count is just off the charts...2 sticks of butter! Yikes!\nHere's what I do:\nI used just 1/2 stick of butter, (unsalted,) and I also use the lower fat cream cheese, (Neufchatel.) I also put the canned tomatoes into the food processor and pulse it a bit, to chop up the tomatoes, and give more consistency to the tomatoes when they are in the dip.\nI use frozen corn, as other do. I just zap it in the micro for about a minute or two. If you can't find white corn, yellow frozen corn works fine.",
            "datePublished": "2011-12-09T22:28:00.910Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "amandak23k"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made on the stovetop because I didn't have an hour to wait for it to cook in the slow cooker. This is good, but would be better with some spice added to it, like sliced pickled jalapenos. I added some onion to it and topped it with sliced jalapenos. Great dip, I used it as a side dish for nachos and tacos.",
            "datePublished": "2010-05-15T07:25:26.787Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "maggie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved it with my changes. I've made this LOTS of times and always get asked for my recipe. First of all, I completely eliminate the butter. You don't need it! Partially drain the rotel, use just regular corn (usually use bag of frozen, just because that's what I have on hand), and MOST IMPORTANT - add chopped pickled jalapeños. Usually at least a half of a cup, but easy to make hotter or milder. Delicious!!!",
            "datePublished": "2016-01-27T20:04:55.533Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ladybuggs5224"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good stuff with tortilla chips. I threw everything into a casserole dish in the oven at 350 and just let it chill while I prepared the rest of dinner. I did add a good bit of cilantro it just felt right and used canned corn because that's what I had on hand but with the many varieties of Rotel available these days you could make all kinds of flavor combinations.",
            "datePublished": "2014-03-22T10:06:26.270Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Veena Mayhak"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added black beans and bacon seasoning. Family really liked it. I only did half batch. It makes alot.",
            "datePublished": "2024-07-15T02:24:57.094Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Alf"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made a half recipe because this makes a lot! I couldn't find white corn so I used yellow. I used salsa instead of tomato, added a bit of shredded Tex mex cheese and a few chopped green onions. Delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-31T20:09:44.510Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "tj2581"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This has become my go-to recipe for carry-ins at work. It is so simple to throw together and everyone loves it! I use one can of regular and 1 can of spicy tomatoes. And only 1/2 cup butter.",
            "datePublished": "2015-12-15T07:46:31.793Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
